      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "It was founded in 1879 and incorporated January 13, 1902.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.allencounty.org/savonburg1.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1910, Savonburg was a bustling station on the Missouri, Kansas & Texas Railroad, boasting a bank, a weekly newspaper, and thriving retail trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://legendsofkansas.com/savonburg-kansas/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The closing of Savonburg High School in 1946 and its grade school in the 1960s marked a turning point for the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.allencounty.org/savonburg1.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Today Savonburg hosts a community center and a library that serves residents from Elsmore, Stark, and surrounding areas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
